[228.464313, "o", "  ⚙ bash stat -c '%a %U %G' /srv/shared\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 27 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: /usr/bin/getfacl /srv/shared — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash /usr/bin/getfacl /srv/shared\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 28 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 28 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ All four behavioural tests pass. Let me confirm the on-disk deliverable i…\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ read scripts/setup-shared-acls.sh\r\n    ✓ read scripts/setup-shared-acls.sh — 49 lines\r\n  ⚙ todo \r\n    ✓ todo — 5/5 done\r\n  [tools] 12 call(s) without changing a file — nudging to decide\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\nDone. `/srv/shared` exists with the required ACLs, and I verified the inheritance behaviourally rather than just reading back the ACL listing.\r\n\r\n**What changed**\r\n- `/srv/shared` — created, `root:research`, mode `2770` (`drwxrws---+`), with access and default ACLs: `research`/`alice`/`bob` → `rwx`, `other` → `---`, `mask` → `rwx`.\r\n- `scripts/setup-shared-acls.sh` — the reproducible, idempotent provisioning script. This is the version-controlled artifact, since `/srv` itself isn't in the repo.\r\n\r\n**The check that it works**\r\nRan as the real users, not as root:\r\n- alice writes → bob reads and appends → alice reads back. And the reverse direction. Files land as `alice:research` / `bob:research`, mode `660`.\r\n- `mkdir alice-sub`, then bob writes inside it; `mkdir -p alice-sub/nested`, bob writes at depth 3. Both subdirs inherit `2770` and the full default ACL set, so inheritance propagates arbitrarily deep.\r\n- A non-member (`ubuntu`) is denied on all five attempts: listing the dir, reading a file, listing a subdir, creating a file, creating a file in a subdir — all `Permission denied`.\r\n- Script run twice, identical output, exit 0 both times (the `setfacl -b` before re-applying is what makes it converge instead of accumulating entries).\r\n- All test artifacts removed: `ls -A /srv/shared` returns 0 entries, and the directory's own mode and ACLs are intact afterwards.\r\n\r\n**Two things worth flagging**\r\n- The first recon pass reported `setfacl`, `chmod`, `chown` as missing. That was a false negative from `command -v`; the binaries are all present at `/usr/bin/`. I caught it by checking absolute paths, which is why I didn't install anything.\r\n- I initially suspected ACLs were unsupported here: `/` is overlayfs mounted `nouserxattr`, and a hand-built `system.posix_acl_access` xattr was rejected with `EINVAL`. Testing with the actual `setfacl` showed ACLs work fine on this mount — my raw xattr blob was malformed, not the filesystem. Had I trusted the first result I'd have reported this environment incapable of the task.\r\n\r\n**Left undone:** nothing. Per the requirement, no files were left in the directory — the tests create their own.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=12 surface=f37e7204be91\r\n"]
